{"version": 1, "sourceSha256": "887cfd3669f99bba383271743d9ca2075f172acdfbce22db6a1391bf118a7107", "documents": [{"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, {"id": "offline-887cfd3669f99bba3832", "filename": "4-Part C.mp3", "sha256": "887cfd3669f99bba383271743d9ca2075f172acdfbce22db6a1391bf118a7107", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-5/887cfd3669f99bba383271743d9ca2075f172acdfbce22db6a1391bf118a7107.mp3", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/887cfd3669f99bba383271743d9ca2075f172acdfbce22db6a1391bf118a7107.json", "format": "mp3", "role": "recording"}], "units": [{"id": "jahshan-1M64tcEX6x5AcPB4_llWo8hUD8lwMDhmC-C-0", "label": "Jahshan set 4 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "pages": [57, 58, 59, 60], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "What does Sandra Morton see as the main aim in her work?\nA to inform patients about the different treatments on offer\nB to publicise the availability of tests for the condition\nC to raise awareness of the symptoms of the illness", "sourcePage": 57, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "When Harry was offered a routine health check at his local surgery, he initially\nA resisted the idea due to his wife’s experience.\nB felt that he was too fit and well to be in need of it.\nC only agreed to attend because his doctor advised him to.", "sourcePage": 57, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "During Harry’s investigations for prostate cancer at a hospital clinic, he\nA felt part of the examination procedure was unpleasant.\nB found it hard to cope with the wait for some results.\nC was given false hope by a preliminary blood test.", "sourcePage": 57, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 34, "prompt": "What was Harry’s response to being diagnosed with prostate cancer?\nA He found himself reacting in a way he hadn’t anticipated.\nB He was unconvinced by the prognosis he was given.\nC He immediately researched treatment options online.", "sourcePage": 58, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "What typical patient response to the illness does Sandra mention?\nA an unwillingness to commence appropriate medication\nB a failure to seek advice regarding different treatment options\nC a reluctance to talk about the embarrassing aspects of treatment", "sourcePage": 58, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "Sandra believes that community follow-up clinics are important because they\nA offer patients more personal aftercare.\nB are proven to be less traumatic for patients.\nC provide rapid treatment for patients developing new symptoms.\nNow look at extract two.\n\nExtract 2: Questions 37-42\nYou hear a neurologist called Dr Frank Madison giving a presentation about the overuse of painkillers.\nYou now have 90 seconds to read questions 37-42.", "sourcePage": 58, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "In Dr Madison’s experience, patients who become addicted to painkillers\nA are more likely to move on to hard drugs.\nB come from a wide variety of backgrounds.\nC usually have existing psychological problems.", "sourcePage": 59, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "Dr Madison thinks some GPs over-prescribe opioid painkillers because these\nA have a long-standing record of success.\nB enable them to deal with patients more quickly.\nC represent a relatively inexpensive form of treatment.", "sourcePage": 59, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "Dr Madison regrets that management of acute pain\nA is often misunderstood by the general public.\nB receives inadequate attention in medical training.\nC fails to distinguish between different possible triggers.", "sourcePage": 59, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "Dr Madison’s main concern about painkillers being readily available is that\nA patients may build up a resistance to them.\nB they may be taken in dangerous amounts by patients.\nC they may interact adversely with patients’ other medication.", "sourcePage": 59, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "Dr Madison refers to the case of an osteoarthritic patient called Ann to highlight\nA the unsuitability of opioids for patients with particular conditions.\nB the effect on patients’ working lives of dependence on painkillers.\nC the extreme fear patients may have of living without pain medication.", "sourcePage": 60, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "Ann’s GP initially failed to identify her dependence because\nA she managed to conceal its physical effects from him.\nB he was unaware that she had another source of drugs.\nC he lacked experience in dealing with problems like hers.\nYou now have two minutes to check your answers.\nTHAT IS THE END OF THE LISTENING TEST", "sourcePage": 60, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 62, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["887cfd3669f99bba383271743d9ca2075f172acdfbce22db6a1391bf118a7107"], "answerSources": [], "matchEvidence": "Exact original recording SHA-256 in the verified Jahshan collection"}]}
